      <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-normal text-gray-900 mb-3">Native vs Cross-Platform App Development</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">When considering app development, one of the most significant decisions revolves around whether to choose native development or cross-platform solutions. Here's a breakdown of both approaches:

### Comparison Table
| Feature                   | Native App Development                | Cross-Platform Development                   |
|---------------------------|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Platforms Supported        | iOS and Android separately            | iOS and Android with a single codebase      |
| Performance                | Optimized performance for each OS     | Moderate performance due to shared code     |
| Development Time           | Longer due to separate codebases      | Typically faster with a shared codebase     |
| UI/UX                     | Highly tailored for each platform     | Consistent across platforms, but less tailored|
| Cost                      | Generally higher due to multiple codebases | Usually lower due to single codebase      |
| Language                   | Swift for iOS, Kotlin/Java for Android| JavaScript/Dart for React Native/Flutter   |

### Summary
Choosing between native and cross-platform development depends on your specific project needs. If you prioritize performance and tailored user experiences, native development might be the way to go. However, for quicker launches and reduced costs, cross-platform solutions like React Native or Flutter can be highly effective.</p>
